    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini-surround\n\n### Description\n\nHello.\r\n\r\nCan the surrounding be highlighted automatically when matching?\r\n\r\nFor example, the text is:\r\n```\r\n\"te_st text\"\r\n```\r\nAnd cursor is on `_`.\r\nIf `sr\"` is pressed, the plugin will highlight the `\"` on both sides.\r\nAnd if `saiw` is pressed, the plugin will highlight `test`.\r\n\r\nWell, it's just like [nvim-surround](https://github.com/kylechui/nvim-surround).\r\nI know this plugin can highlight surrounding with sh, but it needs to be pressed separately, and it can't highlight text object.",
